<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert of Riga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1165–1229</span> · Also known as Albert of Buxhoeveden</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert of Riga was a canon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bremen">Bremen</a> who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonia">Livonia</a> in 1199 and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against the pagan peoples of the eastern Baltic. He founded Riga in 1201 and the military order of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-brothers-of-the-sword">Livonian Brothers of the Sword</a> in 1202. By forcing local leaders to submit and accept baptism, he created the church state of Terra Mariana.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-of-riga.jpg" alt="Albert of Riga" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Artifex · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_of_Riga.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
